-- title:
--   Integral weight-two Hecke algebra is finite over ℤ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Inside the $\mathbb{C}$-algebra $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ of $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms of the space of cusp forms of weight $2$ (the weight being the integer $2$) for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$, consider the set of generators consisting of the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$; the object [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}$-generated by this set, i.e. `Algebra.adjoin ℤ` of it. The assertion is that this subalgebra is a finite, i.e. finitely generated, module over $\mathbb{Z}$. No hypothesis is placed on $S$ beyond its being a set of natural numbers: the primality and divisibility conditions are part of the description of the generators, so the omitted indices are exactly those lying in $S$.
--
--   This is the classical integrality statement that the Hecke algebra of weight-two cusp forms of level $N$, generated over $\mathbb{Z}$ by the $T_\ell$ for $\ell \nmid N$ and the $U_q$ for $q \mid N$ (here with the indices in $S$ discarded), is an order-like finite $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra. It underlies the integrality of Hecke eigenvalues of weight-two eigenforms and is used throughout the level-lowering and modularity-lifting parts of the development, in particular in the construction of ring homomorphisms out of the Hecke algebra and in the analysis of eigenspaces on cohomological carriers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_moduleFinite_heckeAlgebra_two.lean

